\section*{Kaplansky quasitrace additivity conjecture}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
A separable unital algebra is claimed to have normalized 2-quasitraces but no traces; consequently, minimal tensoring can turn two simple unital stably finite C*-algebras into a properly infinite algebra. The cited manuscript argues for that result; its relation to this problem is specified below.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Mathematical claim 1.} OpenAI claims a complex $C^*$-algebra $A$ that is unital and separable and supports a normalized $2$-quasitrace and fixed positive contractions $a,b\in A$ such that every normalized $2$-quasitrace satisfies
\[
\tau(a+b)-\tau(a)-\tau(b)\ge1/144.
\]
Normalized means $\tau(1)=1$; the corner-preserving extension to $M_2(A)$ takes value two on its identity. The positive gap is uniform over all such quasitraces and prevents any of them from being additive tracial states.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Manuscript 1 (family 294, 2026-09-23): Twenty-four bundle-based generators have unit column sum and a strictly smaller row sum, excluding tracial states. Continuous operator scaling preserves this imbalance while nonzero Chern classes obstruct every finite matrix test for proper infiniteness. A bounded-product construction retains all tests simultaneously; established quasitrace and tensor-product implications give the claimed consequences, including a reduced-free-group tensor factor.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Manuscript 1 (family 294, 2026-09-23): The problem selects the mathematical statement summarized here, including its stated hypotheses and parameter range. The cited theorem gives a claimed counterexample to that assertion in full.

\subsection{Formal verification}
For family 294, the scope page documents the following selections. Selections exhibit positive contractions whose normalized quasitraces have a fixed additivity defect, as well as simple stably finite tensor factors with properly infinite spatial product and the corresponding trace failures. The documented statement covers the main claim of manuscript 1. Its selected declaration also covers the clause used for this problem. Comparator files: KaplanskyQuasitrace.lean, KaplanskyStableFiniteness.lean. Declarations: OAI.Kaplansky.kaplansky\_quasitrace\_counterexample, OAI.KaplanskyConsequences.stable\_finiteness\_bundle.

This site has not executed the Lean files or checked their dependencies. These descriptions report the scope of the linked declarations, rather than a new verification of the proofs.

\subsection{Status caveat}
OpenAI attributes these results to an internal model. Its release notice cautions that results lacking full formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently assessed the proofs; a solved label records the scope of the reported claim.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item OpenAI, \emph{A counterexample to Kaplansky's quasitrace conjecture and failure of tensor-product stable finiteness}, 2026-09-23; citation key \texttt{OAI:A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026}. \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (GitHub)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/raw/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{PDF (direct)}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/README.md}{Manuscript page and citation}; \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/main/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/paper.pdf}{Latest version}; Statement source: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-quasitrace-conjecture-September-23-2026/build/01-introduction.tex\#L80}{thm:main}.
\item Family 294: \href{https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/docs/294.md}{Lean scope}.
